| `Dictionary.java` | Interface | Low | High |
| `SourceDictionary.java` | ~100 | Low | High |
| `SetDictionary.java` | ~150 | Medium | High |
| `MapDictionary.java` | ~200 | Medium | High |
| `SpaceDictionary.java` | 120 | HIGH | Critical |
| `SynonymDictionary.java` | ~180 | Medium | High |
| `ProductNameDictionary.java` | 754 | HIGH | Critical |
| `CommonDictionary.java` | ~200 | Medium | High |

### 4.2 Critical Pattern: SpaceDictionary Whitespace Handling

**Java Pattern (SpaceDictionary.java:24,62-65):**
```java
private final static String DELIMITER = "\\s";

@Override
public void addEntry(CharSequence word, Object[] values, List<Object> columnList) {
    String keyword = String.valueOf(values[0]).replaceAll(DELIMITER, "");
    wordSet.add(new CharVector(String.valueOf(keyword), ignoreCase));
    String[] list = String.valueOf(values[0]).split(DELIMITER);
    // ...
}
```

**Kotlin Equivalent:**
```kotlin
companion object {
    private const val DELIMITER = "\\s"
    private val DELIMITER_PATTERN = Regex(DELIMITER)
}

override fun addEntry(word: CharSequence, values: Array<Any?>?, columnList: MutableList<Any>?) {
    if (values.isNullOrEmpty()) return
    val keyword = values[0].toString().replace(DELIMITER_PATTERN, "")
    wordSet.add(CharVector(keyword, ignoreCase))
    val list = values[0].toString().split(DELIMITER_PATTERN)
    // ...
}
```

### 4.3 Critical: Dictionary Key Storage (spaces removed)

This is essential behavior: dictionary keys are stored with ALL spaces removed. The `CharVector.removeWhitespaces()` method is called on keys before storage/lookup.

### Testing Strategy Phase 4:
1. Dictionary loading tests with production dictionary files
2. Key lookup verification with whitespace variants
3. Serialization/deserialization round-trip tests
4. Reload functionality tests

