    |                       |
    |                       +-- ProductNameAnalysisFilter
    |                               |
    |                               +-- ProductNameParsingRule
    |                                       |
    |                                       +-- Rule implementations
```

---

## Specific Interoperability Concerns

### 1. Nullable Types
- Java allows null everywhere; Kotlin requires explicit nullability
- Use `@Nullable` annotations during transition
- Key classes like `CharVector` have nullable array scenarios

### 2. Static Members
- Java static blocks -> Kotlin companion object init
- Java static fields -> Kotlin companion object properties
- Use `@JvmStatic` for Java callers

### 3. Checked Exceptions
- Java `throws IOException` -> Kotlin `@Throws(IOException::class)`
- Lucene API requires exception declarations

### 4. Generic Variance
- Java wildcards (`? extends`, `? super`) -> Kotlin variance (`out`, `in`)
- Collection types need careful conversion

---

### Critical Files for Implementation

1. **`/Users/admin/project/analysis-danuri/src/main/java/com/danawa/util/CharVector.java`** - Core data structure with critical whitespace handling; foundation for all dictionary and analysis operations

2. **`/Users/admin/project/analysis-danuri/src/main/java/com/danawa/search/analysis/korean/KoreanWordExtractor.java`** - Most complex analysis algorithm (914 lines); contains the morphological analysis state machine

3. **`/Users/admin/project/analysis-danuri/src/main/java/com/danawa/search/analysis/product/ProductNameTokenizer.java`** - Entry point for tokenization (534 lines); critical buffer management and type detection

4. **`/Users/admin/project/analysis-danuri/src/main/java/com/danawa/search/analysis/korean/MorphUtil.java`** - Korean character arithmetic with Unicode operations; must preserve exact numeric behavior

5. **`/Users/admin/project/analysis-danuri/src/main/java/com/danawa/search/analysis/dict/SpaceDictionary.java`** - Critical whitespace handling for dictionary entries; defines `\\s` regex splitting behavior
